[b]Balance philosophy[/b]

[b]Skill books are not linear[/b]

Higher-tier books cover increasingly complex material and unlock stronger XP multipliers. Their reading time therefore grows with the depth and usefulness of the knowledge they contain. The tiers are deliberately not distributed through a single linear formula, and different skills do not share an artificial total-page target.

The balance was created by hand using three main references:

[list=1]
[*][b]Real-world book sizes and subject complexity.[/b] Narrow practical guides are usually shorter than complete technical references.
[*][b]The point in a playthrough when a skill is normally used.[/b] Immediate survival knowledge is quicker to access, while advanced industrial knowledge requires a larger investment.
[*][b]The existing in-game book titles.[/b] Titles that imply essential guides, professional instruction, complete techniques, or comprehensive reference works influenced the relative size of each tier.[/list]

[b]Dynamic book weight[/b]

[code]Weight = 0.25 + (0.75 × pages ÷ 220)[/code]

[table=98%][tr][td][b]Example length[/b][/td][td][b]Resulting weight[/b][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]80 pages[/td][td]0.52[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]220 pages[/td][td]1.00[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]352 pages[/td][td]1.45[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]608 pages[/td][td]2.32[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[b]Expansion-mod compatibility[/b]

The mod discovers loaded skill books through Project Zomboid’s item API instead of maintaining a hard-coded list of item IDs. Expansion mods are supported automatically when their books follow the standard game structure:

Books for properly implemented non-canonical skills receive the fallback progression of [b]120 / 220 / 280 / 360 / 440 pages[/b]. Their weight is calculated from those page counts in the same way as canonical books.

[b]What the mod changes[/b]

Only two properties are changed on qualifying skill books:

[list]
[*][code]NumberOfPages[/code]
[*][code]Weight[/code][/list]
The mod does not replace complete vanilla item definitions. Recipe magazines, ordinary books, newspapers, journals, and other literature are not modified.
